HOW TO PLAY

I have shamelessly nicked the instructions from the original, to save writing any myself; they probably evoke more atmosphere than I could muster anyway...


----------------------------------------------

        INSTRUCTIONS
        
          You are the only interceptor
        pilot on board an earth supply
        ship.  The Cylons, determined
        to stop your ship at any cost,
        are sending wave upon wave of
        their attack fleets to blast
        you out of the sky!!
        
          It is entirely up to you to
        defeat them!


        Method of Play
        
          As each wave of Cylon ships
        approaches, you are launched
        from your Mother-ship into
        battle.
        
          When (and IF!!) you manage
        to destroy them all, you must
        return and dock onto your
        Mother-ship where you will be
        refuelled before the next wave
        of Cylons comes to resume the
        attack!!


        Your Instruments
        
          The main view screen fills
        most of your "cockpit"s area,
        with the Long Range Radar sat
        directly above. This shows the
        position of nearby ships which
        are just out of direct view.
        
          Below the main screen, there
        are five instruments showing:
          1: Amount of Shields left
          2: Amount of Fuel left
          3: Rate of Climb
          4: Rate of Turn
          5: Amount of Laser left


        Movements
        
          There are two different key
        layouts (left or right-handed)
        and a joystick option.
        
                   Up Down Left Right
        Option1:   A   Z     <   >
        Option2:   +   >     Z   X
        Option3:    - Joystick -
        
        The keys/joystick control your
        rate of Turn/Climb.
        
               ( H - Hold key )


        Firing the Laser
        
          Your laser is fired by the
        Space-bar on keyboard options
        or the Fire-button on the
        joystick option.
        
          Each shot uses up some of
        your laser energy, which takes
        a short time to recharge.
        
          The laser will not fire if
        there is insufficient energy
        to do so.


        Using the Sights
        
          When you are lined up with a
        Cylon ship, your sights will
        change shape, indicating a
        good chance of a hit.
        
          If they change a second time
        (to a large "X"), then you
        are close enough for the
        targetting system to lock on
        to the enemy Cylon, guiding
        your laser bolts to their
        target.


        Shields
        
          Your shields will protect
        you from the Cylon's missiles
        for a while,  but quickly
        become depleted if you are not
        careful.
        
          You start each wave with a
        full quota of shields, but if
        you run out then you are
        destroyed and the game is over


        Fuel
        
          Your fuel tank is full at
        the start of each wave, but
        will steadily approach empty
        during the game.
          If you run out altogether
        then you will be deemed "Dead
        in space" and the game is over
        However you may return to
        your Mother-ship for extra
        fuel (if available) at any
        time during the game.
          A low-fuel warning bell will
        sound when your fuel level
        falls below a safe margin.


        Your Mother-ship
        
          Your Mother-ship's status
        (shown top/right of cockpit)
        displays the amount of shields
        left, and the number of fuel
        tanks available for emergency
        refuelling in the middle of a
        wave.  There are NO extra
        shields available!
        
          The Mother-ship will only
        come under direct attack when
        you are refuelling, and will
        be destroyed if her shields
        run out.


        Docking
        
          You must dock back on to
        your Mother-ship at the end
        of every wave. You may also
        dock during a wave for extra
        fuel, but not for shields.
        
          To dock, simply line up the
        Mother-ship (coloured Yellow)
        with your sights, and hold
        position until she comes close
        enough for the automatic
        landing sequence to be
        activated.  Be careful not
        to shoot her accidentally!!!


        High Score table
        
          Cylon Attack features a 50
        name high score table, which
        can be saved on disk at the
        end of a game, and reloaded
        the next time you want to play.
          To save the table at the end
        of a session, press BREAK and
        insert a score disk in your
        drive 0.       Then follow the
        instructions on screen.
        
          You may make as many copies
        as you like.


        Competition

          There is a £200 first prize
        for the highest score reached
        on Cylon Attack.

          If you think your best score
        is good enough to win, fill
        in the entry form enclosed
        with the cassette, and return
        it to A&F Software Ltd with a
        Floppy disk   containing your
        saved high score table.
          Only original entry forms
        will be accepted. NO COPIES !!
        Closing date: 1/3/84


        And Finally..
      
          Would you like to see the
        Instructions again before
        loading the main program?

